{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 599 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "996ac35af1f9332345ed6f36d115fa03771d7e8aedff79a00b40a5ab5de358e4" :edb/db-before-t 598 :edb/db-after-t 599 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533911 50 #inst "2026-10-05T11:33:12.378Z" 13194139533911 true] [17592186068688 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265262 13194139533911 true] [17592186073655 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265257 13194139533911 true] [17592186078378 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265269 13194139533911 true] [17592186083147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265279 13194139533911 true] [17592186087708 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265276 13194139533911 true] [17592186115125 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265282 13194139533911 true] [17592186192841 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533911 true] [17592186192841 1145 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{9}{(x-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{9}{(y-2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{9}{(y-2)^{2}} \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{9}{x} \\\\ \\sqrt{(y-2)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{x}} \\\\ |y-2| & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ y-2 & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x}}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the fact that for $y>2,$ we have\n\n$$\n|y-2|=y-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x}}+2.\n$$" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265257 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265258 13194139533911 true] [17592186265257 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265260 13194139533911 true] [17592186265257 1089 "q-216937" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265257 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533911 true] [17592186265257 1100 "The midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(4p,2q)$ and $(-12p,7q)$\n is$\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265257 1113 #uuid "fb752df6-a291-59ef-a8de-b87fa6d272af" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265257 1145 "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(4p,2q)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(-12p,7q)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{4p+(-12p)}{2},\\frac{2q+7q}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-8p}{2},\\frac{9q}{2}) \\\\  & =(-4p,\\frac{9q}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265258 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265259 13194139533911 true] [17592186265258 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533911 true] [17592186265258 1041 "field-1" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265258 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265259 13194139533911 true] [17592186265258 1110 #uuid "bb39ea30-63c6-58a3-a6bc-6778027bdce5" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265259 1034 "-4p" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265259 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265259 1111 #uuid "168fcfde-97c2-537f-9c5c-8d5217483bb4" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265261 13194139533911 true] [17592186265260 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533911 true] [17592186265260 1041 "field-2" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265260 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265261 13194139533911 true] [17592186265260 1110 #uuid "5c5e2fd7-ed0b-5f15-ba68-f6191ae65ceb" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265261 1034 "\\frac{9q}{2}" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265261 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265261 1111 #uuid "60611b3f-ff55-5c5e-8a11-1ab5c3f16a9c" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265262 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265263 13194139533911 true] [17592186265262 1089 "q-29953" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265262 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533911 true] [17592186265262 1100 "Given that $\\frac{14{p}^{3}}{3{q}^{3}}=a$ and  $\\frac{7{p}^{3}}{15{q}^{3}}=b,$ what is the value of $a÷b?$" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265262 1113 #uuid "4305cb9f-6067-5112-8c97-02ae31e17bbe" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265262 1145 "To compute\n\n$$\na÷b=\\frac{14{p}^{3}}{3{q}^{3}}÷\\frac{7{p}^{3}}{15{q}^{3}},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{14{p}^{3}}{3{q}^{3}}÷\\frac{7{p}^{3}}{15{q}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{14{p}^{3}}{3{q}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{15{q}^{3}}{7{p}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot 7{p}^{3}}{3{q}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{5\\cdot 3{q}^{3}}{7{p}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{7{p}^{3}}}{\\cancel{3{q}^{3}}}\\cdot \\frac{5\\cdot \\cancel{3{q}^{3}}}{\\cancel{7{p}^{3}}} & = \\\\ 2\\cdot 5 & = \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265264 13194139533911 true] [17592186265263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265265 13194139533911 true] [17592186265263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265266 13194139533911 true] [17592186265263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265267 13194139533911 true] [17592186265263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265268 13194139533911 true] [17592186265263 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533911 true] [17592186265263 1041 "selection" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265263 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265265 13194139533911 true] [17592186265263 1110 #uuid "89e12d28-1d04-5f40-8eba-010e8968d231" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265264 1034 "\\frac{pq}{10}" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265264 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265264 1111 #uuid "4cee36f1-e329-5709-9e9c-4b4037d4d54a" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265265 1034 "10" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265265 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265265 1111 #uuid "039b90f3-56f7-5935-9183-44582bdb0916" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265266 1034 "\\frac{2p}{5q}" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265266 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265266 1111 #uuid "5331c7c8-ce1c-53c9-b15a-e288dfa655ff" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265267 1034 "5pq" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265267 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265267 1111 #uuid "1c709d77-31cc-5dcb-9ad0-441b69252423" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265268 1034 "2" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265268 1111 #uuid "6a3b0fdc-60ff-570f-add9-1377dc7d635c" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265269 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265270 13194139533911 true] [17592186265269 1089 "q-31365" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265269 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533911 true] [17592186265269 1100 "${x}^{4}-4{y}^{2}=$" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265269 1113 #uuid "629a0494-43df-5f32-9168-213f3c97e24c" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265269 1145 "The difference of squares formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{2}-{b}^{2}=(a+b)(a-b)\n$$\n\nNotice that our expression can be written as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-4{y}^{2}={({x}^{2})}^{2}-(2y)^{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor our expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{({x}^{2})}^{2}-(2y)^{2}=({x}^{2}+2y)({x}^{2}-2y)\n$$" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265271 13194139533911 true] [17592186265270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265272 13194139533911 true] [17592186265270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265273 13194139533911 true] [17592186265270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265274 13194139533911 true] [17592186265270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265275 13194139533911 true] [17592186265270 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533911 true] [17592186265270 1041 "selection" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265270 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265272 13194139533911 true] [17592186265270 1110 #uuid "28be224d-dc1b-5408-805c-ef798603c66f" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265271 1034 "({x}^{2}-2y)^{2}" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265271 1111 #uuid "7bf2f503-8af6-508e-9d50-9c80d05af090" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265272 1034 "({x}^{2}+2y)({x}^{2}-2y)" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265272 1111 #uuid "cc45edde-f92b-5573-a6ab-89be8d2eaabc" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265273 1034 "({x}^{2}-4y)^{2}" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265273 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265273 1111 #uuid "87f346bb-1a98-582b-9d80-5ea115923b7c" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265274 1034 "(x+2y)(x-2y)" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265274 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265274 1111 #uuid "0cc2fc60-0da3-5715-9454-ac86f5d46175" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265275 1034 "({x}^{2}+4y)({x}^{2}-4y)" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265275 1111 #uuid "c8ec8c79-6ab2-5a0d-bcca-b7c6a6fd499a" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265276 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265277 13194139533911 true] [17592186265276 1089 "q-319512" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265276 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533911 true] [17592186265276 1100 "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=-6-5\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265276 1113 #uuid "0de4e360-98e4-5070-8d64-5f82a8a005dd" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265276 1142 true 13194139533911 true] [17592186265276 1145 "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951323/assets/93018ffa3e41f787cf32e4fa9735be8f5c6f9da360361434076cbfaecce51259.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\pi <\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)<\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan\\,(\\frac{5}{6})=0.694\\,738…\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)=\\pi +0.694\\,738…≈3.84,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." 13194139533911 true] [17592186265277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265278 13194139533911 true] [17592186265277 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533911 true] [17592186265277 1041 "field-1" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265277 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265278 13194139533911 true] [17592186265277 1110 #uuid "63185777-fa38-5b11-878a-9df57455d18e" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265278 1034 "3.84" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265278 1111 #uuid "0b80bfad-21f8-5e65-ae12-d79b46b0471c" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265279 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265280 13194139533911 true] [17592186265279 1089 "q-323217" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265279 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533911 true] [17592186265279 1100 "According to the rational root theorem, the polynomial $f(x)=5{x}^{4}+5{x}^{2}-7x+5$ has{{field-1}} *potential* rational roots." 13194139533911 true] [17592186265279 1113 #uuid "acbc7541-07ac-50f0-98b9-4b8cdee191f9" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265279 1145 "Given a polynomial with integer coefficients, the rational roots theorem states that any rational roots of the polynomial must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial:\n\n- The constant term is $5,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1$ and $\\pm 5.$\n\n- The leading coefficient is $5,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1$ and $\\pm 5.$\n\nFirst, we list out all the possibilities for the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm \\frac{1}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{5}, \\\\ \\pm \\frac{5}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{5}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we reduce the fractions to lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{1}{5}, \\\\ \\pm 5, & \\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that some potential roots are duplicates (shown above in red). Removing these duplicates, and listing those remaining in order from least to greatest in absolute value, we have\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{1}{5},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm 5.\n$$\n\nThis makes a total of $6$ potential roots. (Remember that each $\\pm $ sign accounts for $2$ roots, and $2\\cdot 3=6.$)" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265280 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265281 13194139533911 true] [17592186265280 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533911 true] [17592186265280 1041 "field-1" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265280 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265281 13194139533911 true] [17592186265280 1110 #uuid "92ed05e9-0ce6-5e57-b518-667a687d25c9" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265281 1034 "6" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265281 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533911 true] [17592186265281 1111 #uuid "dd3d9c7d-cb4c-5fd2-b954-bb1e42338a66" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265282 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265283 13194139533911 true] [17592186265282 1089 "q-81994" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265282 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533911 true] [17592186265282 1100 "Find the equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $f(x)=-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-2x)+6.$" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265282 1113 #uuid "501a733e-783e-54e0-b097-e7345edc5e15" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265282 1145 "The equation of the vertical asymptote of the function $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is $x=0.$\n\nTo find the equation of the vertical asymptote of $f(x),$ we set the argument of the logarithmic term equal to zero, and solve for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-2x & =0 \\\\ -2x & =-4 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the vertical asymptote is $x=2.$" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265283 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265284 13194139533911 true] [17592186265283 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265285 13194139533911 true] [17592186265283 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265286 13194139533911 true] [17592186265283 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265287 13194139533911 true] [17592186265283 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265288 13194139533911 true] [17592186265283 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533911 true] [17592186265283 1041 "selection" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265283 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265286 13194139533911 true] [17592186265283 1110 #uuid "e2e371c0-c55f-5f7d-ab8b-50efd02a36d8" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265284 1034 "x=1" 13194139533911 true] [17592186265284 1103 #edb/ref